---
import PitchDeck from "../layouts/PitchDeck.astro";
import "../styles/pitch.css";

const slides = [
  "Cover",
  "The Opportunity",
  "The Problem",
  "The Solution",
  "How It Works",
  "Live Demo",
  "Traction",
  "Team",
  "Why We Win",
  "Flywheel",
  "Business Model",
  "Go-to-Market",
  "Financials",
  "Roadmap",
  "The Ask",
];
---

<PitchDeck
  title="Selanet — Pitch Deck"
  description="Frictionless AI-Web Execution Layer"
>
  <!-- Slide Number -->
  <div class="slide-number" id="slideNumber">1 / 15</div>

  <!-- Dot Navigator -->
  <nav class="dot-nav" id="dotNav">
    {
      slides.map((name, i) => (
        <button data-index={i} data-label={name} aria-label={`Go to ${name}`} />
      ))
    }
  </nav>

  <!-- ============================== -->
  <!-- SLIDE CONTAINER                -->
  <!-- ============================== -->
  <div class="deck" id="deck">

    <!-- ============ 1. COVER ============ -->
    <section class="slide slide-cover" data-slide="0">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <h1><a href="https://selanet.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:inherit; text-decoration:none;">Selanet.ai</a></h1>
        <p class="tagline">AI Agent Nodes as Web Infrastructure</p>

        <div class="stats-row">
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="value">2,700+</span>
            <span class="label">Nodes Settled</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="value">90+</span>
            <span class="label">Regions</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="value">30K TXs/day</span>
            <span class="label">On Monad</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 2. THE OPPORTUNITY ============ -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="1">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <span class="badge">Opportunity</span>
        <h2>AI Agents Are Exploding.<br/>The Web Isn't Ready.</h2>
        <p>Every vertical is deploying AI agents — research, sales, support, logistics. But these agents need to access the real web: post-login data, dynamic UIs, multi-step actions.</p>
        <p>Less than 10% of websites offer APIs. The other 90% is locked behind browsers built for humans.</p>

        <div class="stats-row" style="justify-content: flex-start;">
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="value">90%</span>
            <span class="label">of web has no API</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat">
            <span class="value">25–40%</span>
            <span class="label">of agent cost is web access</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 3. THE PROBLEM ============ -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="2">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <span class="badge">Problem</span>
        <h2>Why AI Agents Fail<br/>on the Real Web</h2>
        <p>AI agents access the web like bots — and that breaks at scale.</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Web blocks AI traffic</strong> — Bans, CAPTCHAs, and costs explode at scale. GPTBot and ClaudeBot are frequently blocked.</li>
          <li><strong>Post-login blindness</strong> — Agents can't access data behind authentication — the most valuable data on the web.</li>
          <li><strong>Reliability collapses</strong> — Fragile automation, broken workflows, and data quality issues at scale.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 4. THE SOLUTION ============ -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="3">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <span class="badge">Solution</span>
        <h2>Authenticated, Decentralized<br/>Web Execution &mdash; Live Now</h2>
        <p>Selanet is a decentralized web execution network powered by real users' devices and logged-in sessions. Infrastructure is live across 90+ regions.</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Authenticated & Decentralized</strong> — Real users' logged-in sessions. No centralized IP bottlenecks. Access post-login data that no other provider can reach.</li>
          <li><strong>Native to AI</strong> — Agent-native execution environment with structured data extraction. Open API/SDK for any agent framework.</li>
          <li><strong>Trustless & Verifiable</strong> — Cryptographic proof of execution via zk-TLS. Permissionless participation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 5. HOW IT WORKS ============ -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="4">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <span class="badge">Architecture</span>
        <h2>How It Works</h2>
        <p>AI agents connect to the web through Selanet's distributed node network — real devices, real IPs, real logged-in sessions.</p>

        <div class="flow">
          <span class="flow-step">AI Agent / Client</span>
          <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="flow-step highlight">Selanet Protocol</span>
          <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="flow-step highlight">AI Agent Nodes</span>
          <span class="flow-arrow">&rarr;</span>
          <span class="flow-step">Web / Platforms</span>
        </div>

        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <h3>Node Types</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Desktop Nodes</strong> — Standalone app (Windows, macOS, Linux)</li>
              <li><strong>Mobile Nodes</strong> — Lightweight proxy-based execution</li>
              <li><strong>Data Center Nodes</strong> — High-throughput infrastructure</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Capabilities</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Read</strong> — Extract data from any page</li>
              <li><strong>Act</strong> — Click, scroll, fill forms</li>
              <li><strong>Authenticate</strong> — Post-login access</li>
              <li><strong>Verify</strong> — Cryptographic proof via zk-TLS</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 6. LIVE DEMO ============ -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="5">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <span class="badge">Use Cases</span>
        <h2>Same Question,<br/>Different Result</h2>
        <p>ChatGPT stops at login walls, gets blocked by CAPTCHAs, returns shallow data. Selanet-powered agents execute behind authentication.</p>

        <div class="two-col">
          <div class="case-card">
            <h3>Upflux &mdash; Biz Lead Generation</h3>
            <p class="case-prompt">"Find Korean companies that uses Salesforce"</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>AI Reasoning</strong> — Planning &amp; decision-making</li>
              <li><strong>Real Web Access</strong> — LinkedIn via real user sessions</li>
              <li><strong>Verified Leads</strong> — Enriched from authenticated data</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="case-card">
            <h3>LinqAlpha &mdash; Investment Research</h3>
            <p class="case-prompt">"Analyze trending cosmetics brands on Xiaohongshu"</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Post-login Access</strong> — Xiaohongshu behind auth wall</li>
              <li><strong>Real-time Signals</strong> — Trend data for investment reports</li>
              <li><strong>Geo-specific Data</strong> — China-only platform, local sessions</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <blockquote style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <p>AI can answer questions. <strong>Selanet lets agents execute behind login walls.</strong></p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 7. TRACTION ============ -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="6">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <span class="badge">Traction</span>
        <h2>Live Infrastructure.<br/>Real Pipeline.</h2>

